# Undefined instead of null

In this project, represent missing / empty values with `undefined`, not `null`.

## Rules

- Use `T | undefined` (or optional `T?`) instead of `T | null`
- Initialize empty state with `undefined`, not `null`
- Clear values with `undefined` / omit the property — do not assign `null`
- Prefer `value === undefined` / optional chaining over `value === null` checks
- Do not introduce `null` in new code unless a third-party API requires it at the boundary — map to `undefined` as soon as possible

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const [rate, setRate] = useState<NbrbUsdRate | null>(null);
setError(null);

// ✅ GOOD
const [rate, setRate] = useState<NbrbUsdRate | undefined>(undefined);
setError(undefined);
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
if (error !== null) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
if (error !== undefined) { ... }
```
